+# Automation Control & Safety Runbook
+
+Overview
+- Every automated workflow must verify:
+  - policy evaluation (services/policy/policy_engine.py)
+  - kill switch state (ops/kill_switch/kill_switch.py)
+  - create audit trace (OpenTelemetry) and attestation evidence when performing destructive actions
+
+Kill switch
+- Store kill switch in Vault at path secret/data/aegis/kill_switch with value "on" to pause automation.
+- Example: vault kv put secret/aegis/kill_switch value=on
+
+Emergency stop
+- Operators call: vault kv put secret/aegis/kill_switch value=on
+- All automation entrypoints must call ops/kill_switch/kill_switch.py:is_killed() and abort if True
+
+Policy checks
+- Use services/policy/policy_engine.py to evaluate action permissions and required approvals before execution.
+
+Audit & tracing
+- Ensure services send OTLP traces to the deployed OpenTelemetry collector.
+- Attest rollback and high-risk actions via ops/attestation/attestation_enhanced.py
+
+Approval flows
+- Low-risk actions can be automated if policy allows; high-risk actions require manual signoff (legal/finance) recorded via services/legal/legal_workflow.py
+
